    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9015
    pr_ref:  # 9015
    description: "A detected route framework whose LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORKS detection key differs from its YAML basename has NO route YAML loaded — even when the framework IS detected (manifest or import) — so it emits ZERO routes. Surfaced by the WI-tosul Phase-2 manifest-gating scout (2026-07-07, lab notebook phase2_manifest_gating_scout).\n\nINVARIANT: every framework in `profile.frameworks` resolves to a loadable YAML pattern set (`load_framework_patterns(fw) is not None`).\n\nRoot cause: `framework_patterns.py:903` `_FRAMEWORK_ALIASES` is missing key->basename mappings. Dict-keys `next`/`adonis`/`aspnetcore`/`vert.x`/`zio-http` (as they appear in LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORKS / detection) resolve to NO YAML file (the basenames are `nextjs.yaml`/`adonisjs.yaml`/`aspnet.yaml`/`vertx.yaml`/`zio.yaml`), so `load_framework_patterns` returns None and `enrich_symbols` never applies the route patterns. This is a LATENT bug INDEPENDENT of Phase 2: a Next.js/AdonisJS/ASP.NET/Vert.x/ZIO-http app with a proper manifest still gets its routes silently dropped.\n\nFix: add to `_FRAMEWORK_ALIASES`: next->nextjs, adonis->adonisjs, aspnetcore->aspnet, vert.x->vertx, zio-http->zio (verify each detection key against the actual LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORKS keys before mapping). Add a property test asserting every LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORKS key resolves to a non-None `load_framework_patterns` result (catches future key/basename drift structurally)."  # 9015
    fields:  # 9015
      statement: "Every framework in profile.frameworks resolves to a loadable YAML (load_framework_patterns(fw) is not None), so a detected route framework's route patterns always apply."  # 9015
      root_cause: "framework_patterns.py:903 _FRAMEWORK_ALIASES is missing next->nextjs / adonis->adonisjs / aspnetcore->aspnet / vert.x->vertx / zio-http->zio, so those detection keys resolve to no YAML and enrich_symbols never applies their route patterns."  # 9015
